e event consisted of the shooters firing three sets of 6 shots, with the target visible for 8 seconds.  Ties were broken by 6-shot strings fired in 6 seconds, and then 4 seconds, 3 seconds, and 2 seconds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Of the 18 shooters competing, 12 scored perfect 18s in the opening round, contested over 8-second strings.  The 6-second string did little to break the tie, as only " [:a {:href "/athletes/44631"} "Thomas Carr"] " (USA) failed to hit all 6 targets and was eliminated.  In the 4-second string, six shooters scored perfect 6s and five shooters were eliminated.  All three of the Italian shooters advanced to the next stage.  " [:a {:href "/athletes/42994"} "Renzo Morigi"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/42990"} "Domenico Matteucci"] " were joined by Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/42540"} "Heinz Hax"] " in hitting all six targets in 3 seconds, and they contested the final competition over 2 seconds.  Morigi again recorded a perfect score to win the gold medal, hitting his final target as it was turning away, with Hax taking second with 4 targets, and Matteucci third with 3 targets."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Most of the foreign shooters came with German Walther and Spanish Star pistols but, after watching the Americans using .22 Colt Woodsman pistols, they all went and bought that pistol, and it was used by all shooters in the competition."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "8 second Round"] [:th {} "6 second Round"] [:th {} "4 second Round"] [:th {} "3 second Round"] [:th {} "2 second Round"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/42994"} "Renzo Morigi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "42"] [:td {} "18"] [:td {} "6"] [:td {} "6"] [:td